      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The rise of obesity in the UK has led to greater numbers of patients requiring bariatric surgery. This article provides an overview of the two main types of surgery available: laparoscopic adjustable gastric band and Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery. The nurse's role in pre-operative assessment and post-operative care are discussed. Strategies to maintain weight loss are suggested to ensure optimum outcomes of surgery and to improve patients' quality of life."},
